    cautions: "The plant is safe, but the main field risk is misidentifying young spring shoots: toxic dogbane (Apocynum) shoots emerge in similar habitat. Reject any shoot with milky sap, a very bitter/acrid taste, or paired (opposite) leaves/branching. Mature fireweed leaves consumed in large amounts have a mild laxative effect.",
